 "text": "Hi! How are you doing right now? I' so glad you asked. Early dementia can be challenging for both the person and their family. Has he been consistent with any routine, like going for walks? Try to stick familiar routes and ask about well remembered places. A local history museum could work well. Yes, and keep them short and simple. A coffee shop with a view he sees from the window is calming. A museum gives lots of familiar sights without tired floors. Be honest about it. He might appreciate you' being real about how hard it is.",
